---@field ClusterSubnetGroupName? aws.redshift.String The name of a cluster subnet group to be associated with this cluster.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.redshift.String The EC2 Availability Zone (AZ) in which you want Amazon Redshift to provision the cluster. For example, if you have several EC2 instances running in a specific Availability Zone, then you might want the cluster to be provisioned in the same zone in order to decrease network latency.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.redshift.String The weekly time range (in UTC) during which automated cluster maintenance can occur.
---@field ClusterParameterGroupName? aws.redshift.String The name of the parameter group to be associated with this cluster.
---@field AutomatedSnapshotRetentionPeriod? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The number of days that automated snapshots are retained. If the value is 0, automated snapshots are disabled. Even if automated snapshots are disabled, you can still create manual snapshots when you want with CreateClusterSnapshot.
---@field ManualSnapshotRetentionPeriod? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The default number of days to retain a manual snapshot. If the value is -1, the snapshot is retained indefinitely. This setting doesn't change the retention period of existing snapshots.
---@field Port? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The port number on which the cluster accepts incoming connections.
---@field ClusterVersion? aws.redshift.String The version of the Amazon Redshift engine software that you want to deploy on the cluster.
---@field AllowVersionUpgrade? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional If true, major version upgrades can be applied during the maintenance window to the Amazon Redshift engine that is running on the cluster.
---@field NumberOfNodes? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The number of compute nodes in the cluster. This parameter is required when the ClusterType parameter is specified as multi-node.
---@field PubliclyAccessible? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional If true, the cluster can be accessed from a public network.
---@field Encrypted? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional If true, the data in the cluster is encrypted at rest. If you set the value on this parameter to false, the request will fail.
---@field HsmClientCertificateIdentifier? aws.redshift.String Specifies the name of the HSM client certificate the Amazon Redshift cluster uses to retrieve the data encryption keys stored in an HSM.
---@field HsmConfigurationIdentifier? aws.redshift.String Specifies the name of the HSM configuration that contains the information the Amazon Redshift cluster can use to retrieve and store keys in an HSM.
---@field ElasticIp? aws.redshift.String The Elastic IP (EIP) address for the cluster.
---@field Tags? aws.redshift.TagList A list of tag instances.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.redshift.String The Key Management Service (KMS) key ID of the encryption key that you want to use to encrypt data in the cluster.
---@field EnhancedVpcRouting? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional An option that specifies whether to create the cluster with enhanced VPC routing enabled. To create a cluster that uses enhanced VPC routing, the cluster must be in a VPC. For more information, see Enhanced VPC Routing in the Amazon Redshift Cluster Management Guide.
---@field AdditionalInfo? aws.redshift.String Reserved.
---@field IamRoles? aws.redshift.IamRoleArnList A list of Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles that can be used by the cluster to access other Amazon Web Services services. You must supply the IAM roles in their Amazon Resource Name (ARN) format.
---@field MaintenanceTrackName? aws.redshift.String An optional parameter for the name of the maintenance track for the cluster. If you don't provide a maintenance track name, the cluster is assigned to the current track.
---@field SnapshotScheduleIdentifier? aws.redshift.String A unique identifier for the snapshot schedule.
---@field AvailabilityZoneRelocation? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional The option to enable relocation for an Amazon Redshift cluster between Availability Zones after the cluster is created.
---@field AquaConfigurationStatus? aws.redshift.AquaConfigurationStatus|string This parameter is retired. It does not set the AQUA configuration status. Amazon Redshift automatically determines whether to use AQUA (Advanced Query Accelerator).
---@field DefaultIamRoleArn? aws.redshift.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the IAM role that was set as default for the cluster when the cluster was created.
---@field LoadSampleData? aws.redshift.String A flag that specifies whether to load sample data once the cluster is created.
---@field ManageMasterPassword? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional If true, Amazon Redshift uses Secrets Manager to manage this cluster's admin credentials. You can't use MasterUserPassword if ManageMasterPassword is true. If ManageMasterPassword is false or not set, Amazon Redshift uses MasterUserPassword for the admin user account's password.
---@field MasterPasswordSecretKmsKeyId? aws.redshift.String The ID of the Key Management Service (KMS) key used to encrypt and store the cluster's admin credentials secret. You can only use this parameter if ManageMasterPassword is true.
---@field IpAddressType? aws.redshift.String The IP address types that the cluster supports. Possible values are ipv4 and dualstack.
---@field MultiAZ? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional If true, Amazon Redshift will deploy the cluster in two Availability Zones (AZ).
---@field RedshiftIdcApplicationArn? aws.redshift.String The Amazon resource name (ARN) of the Amazon Redshift IAM Identity Center application.
---@field CatalogName? aws.redshift.CatalogNameString The name of the Glue data catalog that will be associated with the cluster enabled with Amazon Redshift federated permissions.
---@field ExtraComputeForAutomaticOptimization? aws.redshift.BooleanOptional If true, allocates additional compute resources for running automatic optimization operations.

