---Describes the result of a cluster resize operation.
---@class aws.redshift.ResizeProgressMessage
---@field TargetNodeType? aws.redshift.String The node type that the cluster will have after the resize operation is complete.
---@field TargetNumberOfNodes? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The number of nodes that the cluster will have after the resize operation is complete.
---@field TargetClusterType? aws.redshift.String The cluster type after the resize operation is complete.
---@field Status? aws.redshift.String The status of the resize operation.
---@field ImportTablesCompleted? aws.redshift.ImportTablesCompleted The names of tables that have been completely imported .
---@field ImportTablesInProgress? aws.redshift.ImportTablesInProgress The names of tables that are being currently imported.
---@field ImportTablesNotStarted? aws.redshift.ImportTablesNotStarted The names of tables that have not been yet imported.
---@field AvgResizeRateInMegaBytesPerSecond? aws.redshift.DoubleOptional The average rate of the resize operation over the last few minutes, measured in megabytes per second. After the resize operation completes, this value shows the average rate of the entire resize operation.
---@field TotalResizeDataInMegaBytes? aws.redshift.LongOptional The estimated total amount of data, in megabytes, on the cluster before the resize operation began.
---@field ProgressInMegaBytes? aws.redshift.LongOptional While the resize operation is in progress, this value shows the current amount of data, in megabytes, that has been processed so far. When the resize operation is complete, this value shows the total amount of data, in megabytes, on the cluster, which may be more or less than TotalResizeDataInMegaBytes (the estimated total amount of data before resize).
---@field ElapsedTimeInSeconds? aws.redshift.LongOptional The amount of seconds that have elapsed since the resize operation began. After the resize operation completes, this value shows the total actual time, in seconds, for the resize operation.
---@field EstimatedTimeToCompletionInSeconds? aws.redshift.LongOptional The estimated time remaining, in seconds, until the resize operation is complete. This value is calculated based on the average resize rate and the estimated amount of data remaining to be processed. Once the resize operation is complete, this value will be 0.
---@field ResizeType? aws.redshift.String An enum with possible values of ClassicResize and ElasticResize. These values describe the type of resize operation being performed.
---@field Message? aws.redshift.String An optional string to provide additional details about the resize action.
---@field TargetEncryptionType? aws.redshift.String The type of encryption for the cluster after the resize is complete.
---@field DataTransferProgressPercent? aws.redshift.DoubleOptional The percent of data transferred from source cluster to target cluster.

