---Describes a snapshot.
---@class aws.redshift.Snapshot
---@field SnapshotIdentifier? aws.redshift.String The snapshot identifier that is provided in the request.
---@field ClusterIdentifier? aws.redshift.String The identifier of the cluster for which the snapshot was taken.
---@field SnapshotCreateTime? aws.redshift.TStamp The time (in UTC format) when Amazon Redshift began the snapshot. A snapshot contains a copy of the cluster data as of this exact time.
---@field Status? aws.redshift.String The snapshot status. The value of the status depends on the API operation used:
---@field Port? aws.redshift.Integer The port that the cluster is listening on.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.redshift.String The Availability Zone in which the cluster was created.
---@field ClusterCreateTime? aws.redshift.TStamp The time (UTC) when the cluster was originally created.
---@field MasterUsername? aws.redshift.String The admin user name for the cluster.
---@field ClusterVersion? aws.redshift.String The version ID of the Amazon Redshift engine that is running on the cluster.
---@field EngineFullVersion? aws.redshift.String The cluster version of the cluster used to create the snapshot. For example, 1.0.15503.
---@field SnapshotType? aws.redshift.String The snapshot type. Snapshots created using CreateClusterSnapshot and CopyClusterSnapshot are of type "manual".
---@field NodeType? aws.redshift.String The node type of the nodes in the cluster.
---@field NumberOfNodes? aws.redshift.Integer The number of nodes in the cluster.
---@field DBName? aws.redshift.String The name of the database that was created when the cluster was created.
---@field VpcId? aws.redshift.String The VPC identifier of the cluster if the snapshot is from a cluster in a VPC. Otherwise, this field is not in the output.
---@field Encrypted? aws.redshift.Boolean If true, the data in the snapshot is encrypted at rest.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.redshift.String The Key Management Service (KMS) key ID of the encryption key that was used to encrypt data in the cluster from which the snapshot was taken.
---@field EncryptedWithHSM? aws.redshift.Boolean A boolean that indicates whether the snapshot data is encrypted using the HSM keys of the source cluster. true indicates that the data is encrypted using HSM keys.
---@field AccountsWithRestoreAccess? aws.redshift.AccountsWithRestoreAccessList A list of the Amazon Web Services accounts authorized to restore the snapshot. Returns null if no accounts are authorized. Visible only to the snapshot owner.
---@field OwnerAccount? aws.redshift.String For manual snapshots, the Amazon Web Services account used to create or copy the snapshot. For automatic snapshots, the owner of the cluster. The owner can perform all snapshot actions, such as sharing a manual snapshot.
---@field TotalBackupSizeInMegaBytes? aws.redshift.Double The size of the complete set of backup data that would be used to restore the cluster.
---@field ActualIncrementalBackupSizeInMegaBytes? aws.redshift.Double The size of the incremental backup.
---@field BackupProgressInMegaBytes? aws.redshift.Double The number of megabytes that have been transferred to the snapshot backup.
---@field CurrentBackupRateInMegaBytesPerSecond? aws.redshift.Double The number of megabytes per second being transferred to the snapshot backup. Returns 0 for a completed backup.
---@field EstimatedSecondsToCompletion? aws.redshift.Long The estimate of the time remaining before the snapshot backup will complete. Returns 0 for a completed backup.
---@field ElapsedTimeInSeconds? aws.redshift.Long The amount of time an in-progress snapshot backup has been running, or the amount of time it took a completed backup to finish.
---@field SourceRegion? aws.redshift.String The source region from which the snapshot was copied.
---@field Tags? aws.redshift.TagList The list of tags for the cluster snapshot.
---@field RestorableNodeTypes? aws.redshift.RestorableNodeTypeList The list of node types that this cluster snapshot is able to restore into.
---@field EnhancedVpcRouting? aws.redshift.Boolean An option that specifies whether to create the cluster with enhanced VPC routing enabled. To create a cluster that uses enhanced VPC routing, the cluster must be in a VPC. For more information, see Enhanced VPC Routing in the Amazon Redshift Cluster Management Guide.
---@field MaintenanceTrackName? aws.redshift.String The name of the maintenance track for the snapshot.
---@field ManualSnapshotRetentionPeriod? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The number of days that a manual snapshot is retained. If the value is -1, the manual snapshot is retained indefinitely.
---@field ManualSnapshotRemainingDays? aws.redshift.IntegerOptional The number of days until a manual snapshot will pass its retention period.
---@field SnapshotRetentionStartTime? aws.redshift.TStamp A timestamp representing the start of the retention period for the snapshot.
---@field MasterPasswordSecretArn? aws.redshift.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the cluster's admin user credentials secret.
---@field MasterPasswordSecretKmsKeyId? aws.redshift.String The ID of the Key Management Service (KMS) key used to encrypt and store the cluster's admin credentials secret.
